---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const hosts = [
  { anchor: 'github-pages', name: 'GitHub Pages', target: 'username.github.io' },
  { anchor: 'cloudflare-pages', name: 'Cloudflare Pages', target: 'project.pages.dev' },
  { anchor: 'vercel', name: 'Vercel', target: 'project.vercel.app' },
  { anchor: 'netlify', name: 'Netlify', target: 'site.netlify.app' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Connect your subdomain · filipino-talent.com"
  description="The last step: tell GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages, Vercel, or Netlify to answer for your new filipino-talent.com subdomain."
>
<section>
  <span class="tag">Final step</span>
  <h1>Connect your subdomain</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Your subdomain is published, but that is only half the job. DNS tells the
    internet where to look; your host also has to agree to answer for your new
    address. Until you do this, opening
    <code>https://yourname.filipino-talent.com</code> shows an error (Cloudflare
    Pages shows <strong>522 Connection timed out</strong>; others show a 404 or a
    host error page).
  </p>
  <p class="lead">
    Pick the host where your portfolio lives and follow the steps. It takes
    about a minute.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="grid" style="margin-top:24px">
  {hosts.map((h) => (
    <a class="card" href={`#${h.anchor}`} style="text-decoration:none">
      <strong style="color:var(--text)">{h.name}</strong>
      <div class="muted mono" style="font-size:.82rem;margin-top:6px">{h.target}</div>
      <div style="margin-top:8px;font-size:.9rem">Go to steps →</div>
    </a>
  ))}
</div>

<div class="notice warn" style="margin-top:24px">
  <strong>Using Wix, Canva, WordPress, or another builder?</strong>
  This service only connects hosts that let you attach a custom domain for free
  through a plain CNAME. Wix needs a paid plan and its own DNS records, so it is
  not supported here. Move your page to <a href="#github-pages">GitHub Pages</a>,
  <a href="#cloudflare-pages">Cloudflare Pages</a>, <a href="#vercel">Vercel</a>,
  or <a href="#netlify">Netlify</a> — all free — then come back to this page.
</div>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2 id="github-pages" style="margin-top:0">GitHub Pages</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Open your repository, then go to <strong>Settings → Pages</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Under <strong>Custom domain</strong>, type
      <code>yourname.filipino-talent.com</code> and click <strong>Save</strong>.
      GitHub adds a <code>CNAME</code> file to your repository.
    </li>
    <li>
      Wait a few minutes. GitHub runs a DNS check and shows a green checkmark
      when it finds the record we published.
    </li>
    <li>
      Once it passes, tick <strong>Enforce HTTPS</strong>. The certificate can
      take up to an hour the first time.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Notes:</strong> one custom domain per Pages site. For a project site
    (<code>username.github.io/reponame</code>), the subdomain still routes to
    that repository. Do not add the <code>CNAME</code> file before we publish
    DNS — it is already published by the time you reach this step.
  </div>
</section>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2 id="cloudflare-pages" style="margin-top:0">Cloudflare Pages</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Open your Pages project in the Cloudflare dashboard.
    </li>
    <li>
      Go to <strong>Custom domains → Set up a custom domain</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Enter <code>yourname.filipino-talent.com</code> and continue.
    </li>
    <li>
      Cloudflare finds the CNAME we already published and verifies it
      automatically. Click <strong>Activate domain</strong> if it asks.
    </li>
    <li>
      Wait for the certificate (usually a few minutes, up to an hour).
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="notice warn">
    <strong>Seeing 522 Connection timed out?</strong> That means this step is not
    done yet. Add the subdomain under <strong>Custom domains</strong> and the
    error clears. If Cloudflare asks you to "add a CNAME record", it is already
    done by us — just continue.
  </div>
</section>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2 id="vercel" style="margin-top:0">Vercel</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Open your project, then go to <strong>Settings → Domains</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Click <strong>Add Domain</strong> and enter
      <code>yourname.filipino-talent.com</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Vercel shows the record it expects. If it shows the record as valid, you
      are done — wait for the certificate.
    </li>
    <li>
      If Vercel says <strong>Invalid Configuration</strong>, it may want a
      project-specific CNAME (for example
      <code>xxxx.vercel-dns-017.com</code>). Email
      <a href="mailto:verify@filipino-talent.com">verify@filipino-talent.com</a>
      with the value it shows and we will update your record.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Notes:</strong> Vercel may also ask you to verify ownership with a
    TXT record. If so, email us and we will help.
  </div>
</section>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2 id="netlify" style="margin-top:0">Netlify</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Open your site, then go to <strong>Domain management → Add a domain</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Enter <code>yourname.filipino-talent.com</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose to keep DNS outside Netlify — the "I already own this domain" path.
      Do <strong>not</strong> switch to Netlify DNS; that would mean changing
      nameservers, which this service cannot do.
    </li>
    <li>
      Netlify finds the CNAME we published and verifies it. Wait for the HTTPS
      certificate.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Notes:</strong> if Netlify shows "Awaiting External DNS" for more
    than 15 minutes, wait a little longer — the record is already live, so this
    is usually just propagation.
  </div>
</section>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">Still not working?</h2>
  <p>
    Give it 10–15 minutes after DNS is published, then reload in a private
    window. If it is still broken, see
    <a href="/guide/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>, or email
    <a href="mailto:verify@filipino-talent.com">verify@filipino-talent.com</a>
    with your subdomain and the host you use.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/guide">Back to the guide</a>
  </p>
</section>
</Base>
